WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:07.205
"You've found Hosmer Angel? Where?" shouted Mr. Windibank, looking frantically around the room like an animal caught in a trap.

2
00:00:07.206 --> 00:00:13.293
"There's no escaping, Mr. Windibank," said Sherlock Holmes. "Sit down and let's talk this over."

3
00:00:13.294 --> 00:00:21.442
Our visitor collapsed in a chair with a ghastly look on his face and beads of sweat on his brow. "I've done nothing illegal!" he said defiantly.

4
00:00:21.443 --> 00:00:27.783
"That's right; nothing you did was illegal. But you played a heartless and selfish trick," said Holmes.

5
00:00:27.784 --> 00:00:31.861
"Now let me run through the series of events, and you can contradict me if I'm wrong."

6
00:00:31.862 --> 00:00:38.439
Mr. Windibank huddled in his chair like someone who was utterly crushed. Holmes sat down and rested his feet on the hearth.

7
00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:43.011
"A man married a much older woman for her money," began Holmes.

8
00:00:43.012 --> 00:00:47.186
"He also had the use of his stepdaughter's money for as long as she lived with them.

9
00:00:47.187 --> 00:00:53.605
The money was a considerable sum for people in their position, and the loss of it would have made a serious difference in their lifestyle."

10
00:00:53.606 --> 00:00:59.842
Mr. Windibank said nothing, so Holmes continued the story. The stepdaughter was a kind and friendly person.

11
00:00:59.843 --> 00:01:04.912
With her income and her outgoing personality, it was obvious that she would not remain single for long.

12
00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:11.586
Her stepfather needed to take action, so he kept her at home and prevented her from having any contact with people her own age.

13
00:01:11.587 --> 00:01:17.820
But he soon found that this would not solve the problem forever. The young woman became impatient and restless at home.

14
00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:23.580
She insisted upon her rights and finally announced that she would be attending the plumbers' ball with her mother.

15
00:01:23.581 --> 00:01:31.652
"What did her clever stepfather do then?" asked Holmes. "With the assistance of his wife, he disguised himself as Hosmer Angel.

16
00:01:31.653 --> 00:01:38.890
He covered his keen eyes with tinted glasses, masked his face with a mustache and bushy whiskers, and reduced his voice to a whisper."

17
00:01:38.891 --> 00:01:43.739
"And Miss Sutherland's poor eyesight made it even easier for the disguise to work," I said.

18
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:50.047
"Exactly!" said Holmes. "The stepfather kept men away from her by pretending to court her himself."

19
00:01:50.048 --> 00:01:56.047
"It was only a joke at first," groaned Windibank. "We never thought that she'd fall for it so completely."

20
00:01:56.048 --> 00:02:06.713
"But she did," said Holmes. "She believed that her stepfather was in France, so there was no reason to suspect him. She was flattered by Mr. Angel's attentions.

21
00:02:06.714 --> 00:02:10.861
Her mother increased the effect by enthusiastically approving of Mr. Angel."

22
00:02:10.862 --> 00:02:15.288
Holmes said that after the ball it was essential for Mr. Angel to call on Miss Sutherland.

23
00:02:15.289 --> 00:02:19.526
It was obvious to her stepfather that the matter should be pushed as far as possible.

24
00:02:19.527 --> 00:02:23.533
An engagement would keep her—and her money—safe from any other men.

25
00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:30.193
"But the deception could not be maintained forever," said Holmes. "Those pretend journeys to France were rather awkward.

26
00:02:30.194 --> 00:02:35.510
It was clearly time to end the business in a dramatic way that would leave a huge impression on the young woman.

27
00:02:35.511 --> 00:02:39.434
She had to be prevented from thinking about other suitors for a long time."

28
00:02:39.435 --> 00:02:44.418
So on their wedding day, Hosmer Angel mentioned that something ominous might happen.

29
00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:48.411
And he made Miss Sutherland swear on a Bible that she would always be true to him.

30
00:02:48.412 --> 00:02:56.991
"You wanted Miss Sutherland to be tied to Hosmer Angel and so uncertain about his fate that she would not look at another man for many years," said Holmes.

31
00:02:56.992 --> 00:03:02.244
"So you conveniently disappeared by the old trick of stepping into one door of a carriage and out the other.

32
00:03:02.245 --> 00:03:06.482
I think that was the chain of events, Mr. Windibank! Don't you agree?"

33
00:03:06.483 --> 00:03:13.905
Our visitor had recovered some of his confidence while Holmes had been talking. Now he rose from his chair with a bitter sneer on his face.

34
00:03:13.906 --> 00:03:17.976
"It may be the chain of events, or it may not be, Mr. Holmes," he said.

35
00:03:17.977 --> 00:03:22.730
"But if you're so smart, you should be smart enough to know that you are the one breaking the law now.

36
00:03:22.731 --> 00:03:29.475
I have done nothing illegal from the beginning, but as long as you keep the door locked, I could sue you for assault and unlawful restraint."

37
00:03:29.476 --> 00:03:34.387
"As you say, the law cannot touch you." Holmes unlocked and threw open the door.

38
00:03:34.388 --> 00:03:41.211
"But there was never a man who deserved punishment more. If the young lady had a brother or a friend, he ought to horsewhip you."

39
00:03:41.212 --> 00:03:46.462
Mr. Windibank continued to sneer at Holmes, which brought a flush of anger to the detective's face.

40
00:03:46.463 --> 00:03:51.873
"It is not part of my duties to my client, but here's a riding crop, and I think I'll just use it."

41
00:03:51.874 --> 00:03:58.031
Holmes took two swift steps toward the whip, but before he could grasp it, Mr. Windibank dashed out of the room.

42
00:03:58.032 --> 00:04:05.187
With a loud clatter, he ran down the steps and out the front door. From the window we could see him running at top speed down the street.

43
00:04:05.188 --> 00:04:11.345
"He's a cold-blooded scoundrel," said Holmes, laughing as he threw himself down on the chair once more.

44
00:04:11.346 --> 00:04:17.170
"That fellow will get away with this act, but eventually he'll commit a crime so bad he'll wind up on the gallows.

45
00:04:17.171 --> 00:04:20.503
This case has had some interesting points to it after all."

46
00:04:20.504 --> 00:04:24.170
"I still can't follow all the steps in your reasoning," I said.

47
00:04:24.171 --> 00:04:30.255
"It was obvious that this Mr. Hosmer Angel must have had a strong motive for his strange behavior," said Holmes.

48
00:04:30.256 --> 00:04:35.156
"And it was equally clear that the only man who profited from the incident was the stepfather.

49
00:04:35.157 --> 00:04:42.068
The two men were never in the same place at the same time. In fact, Angel only appeared when Windibank was away."

50
00:04:42.069 --> 00:04:47.234
Holmes explained that the tinted glasses, whiskers, and strange voice all suggested a disguise.

51
00:04:47.235 --> 00:04:53.905
His suspicions were confirmed when Angel typed not only his letters to Miss Sutherland but also his signature.

52
00:04:53.906 --> 00:05:00.817
"This suggested that his handwriting was so familiar to Miss Sutherland that she would recognize even the smallest sample," said Holmes.

53
00:05:00.818 --> 00:05:05.555
"But how did you prove that Windibank and Angel were the same man?" I wanted to know.

54
00:05:05.556 --> 00:05:13.309
"Miss Sutherland had provided us with the name of her stepfather's employer—the wine importers Westhouse and Marbank of Fenchurch Street," said Holmes.

55
00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:20.045
"I wrote to Windibank at that address, asking him to come here. As I expected, his reply was typewritten.

56
00:05:20.046 --> 00:05:24.790
The individual letters looked exactly the same as those in Angel's notes to Miss Sutherland."

57
00:05:24.791 --> 00:05:32.534
Holmes took his investigation one step further. He started with the description of Hosmer Angel in Miss Sutherland's newspaper ad.

58
00:05:32.535 --> 00:05:37.777
Then he eliminated all the elements that could be a disguise—the glasses, whiskers, and voice.

59
00:05:37.778 --> 00:05:44.522
Finally he wrote a letter to the owners of Westhouse and Marbank, asking if they had any employees who matched that description.

60
00:05:44.523 --> 00:05:50.521
"In the same mail with Windibank's reply, I received a response from the wine importers," said Holmes.

61
00:05:50.522 --> 00:05:56.028
"They said that my description exactly matched one of their employees—Mr. James Windibank."

62
00:05:56.029 --> 00:06:02.321
The case was closed, but I had one more question. "What about Miss Sutherland? Will you tell her?"

63
00:06:02.322 --> 00:06:08.677
Holmes sighed. "She won't believe me, Watson. Miss Sutherland is in love with 'Mr. Hosmer Angel.'

64
00:06:08.678 --> 00:06:15.582
She would rather delude herself about him than accept the fact that he never actually existed."

